## How this corpus is verified

`tools/corpus_extract.py` lifts the cited paragraphs out of the vaulted bytes.
`tools/citecheck.py` then audits the engine against them, and the two share no
extraction code — a checker that can regenerate what it is checking reproduces
its own bug on both sides and agrees with itself.

281 checks run on every build, across four fronts: the vault hashes as recorded,
every citation resolves to a transcribed clause whose own paragraph designator
matches the citation, every published figure appears in the text of the clause
cited *for it*, and any span the engine wraps in curly quotes is verbatim in the
source. `py tools/citecheck.py --selftest` mutates the engine and the vault six
ways and requires each to be caught.
